    "body": "## Summary\n- anchor stale refund recovery's 23h Stripe idempotency safety window to immutable refund request creation time instead of mutable `updatedAt`\n- prevent dispatch/retry/recovery timestamp refreshes from extending the automatic retry deadline\n- add a focused regression test proving a 24h-old refund request cannot become retry-safe merely because its latest dispatch timestamp is fresh\n\n## Safety rationale\n`updatedAt` changes on `startDispatch()` and `reschedule()`. Using it as the Stripe idempotency safety clock allowed each retry/recovery cycle to move the effective deadline forward. `createdAt` is immutable, so the gate is monotonic and intentionally fail-closed: unusually delayed first attempts may be quarantined earlier, but ambiguous provider operations cannot be automatically retried outside the configured safety window.\n\n## Validation\n- focused regression coverage added\n- full exact-head GitHub Actions required before merge",
